    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0146" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/9–244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé Near the Greek Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Shantz</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-02">September 2,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received September 2—2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek 281. The EAM representatives reached Cairo August 31. Following Ministers
                    were sworn in this noon: Svolos Finance with Angelopoulos Under Minister;
                    Askoutsis Communications; Tsirimokos National Economy; Porphyrogennis Labor and
                    Zevghos Agriculture.</p>
                <p>Repeated to AmPolAd<anchor n="16" xml:id="d140-f1"/> Caserta as number 40.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shantz</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d140-f1" n="16" xml:id="d140-f1-content">
                <p>American Political Adviser, Staff of the Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean,
                    with headquarters at Caserta, Italy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
